From and after the time when the planning commission shall have organized and selected its officers, and shall have adopted its rules of procedure, then said planning commission shall have the following powers, duties, and responsibilities:
(1) To make careful and comprehensive surveys and studies of existing conditions and probable future developments and to prepare amendments or updates to the Joint Comprehensive Plan for Pickens County, which was adopted on July 30, 1993, also known as the official plan, and a short term work program update adopted December 23, 1998; for physical, social, environmental, and economic growth as will promote the development of Pickens County; such plan(s), with accompanying maps, plats, charts, and descriptive materials, shall show the planning commission's recommendations for the physical development and uses of land, shall meet the minimum requirements of the Georgia Planning Act of 1989 and related minimum planning standards and procedures promulgated by the state, and may include other matters of special interest to Pickens County;
(2) To prepare and recommend to the Pickens County Commissioner from time to time, such changes in the plan or any part thereof as may be deemed necessary by the commissioner or by the planning commission; to prepare and recommend to the Pickens County Commissioner from time to time plans and/or recommendations for specific improvements in pursuance of the official plan;
(3) To cooperate with other municipal or regional planning commissions and other agencies or groups to further the local planning program and to assure harmonious and integrated planning for the area;
(4) To prepare and recommend for adoption by the Pickens County Commissioner amendments to the Pickens County Land Development Ordinance, which may deal with such matters as establishing land use districts and regulations, regulations for the subdivision of land, sign controls, flood protection, environmental protection, soil erosion and sediment control, manufactured home development standards, and other regulations that would be for the benefit of managing growth in Pickens County; and to oversee the administration of the regulations that may be adopted or amended;
(5) To prepare and recommend for adoption by the Pickens County Commissioner an official map showing the location of existing and proposed streets, public open spaces, and public building sites within Pickens County;
(6) To delegate to employees authority to perform ministerial acts, in all cases except where final action of the planning commission is necessary;
(7) If deemed advisable, to establish an advisory committee or committees; and,
(8) To arrange or conduct any form of publicity relative to planning commission activities for the general purpose of public understanding,
(Ord. of 12-10-99, § 3)

