When establishing, maintaining or changing charges for any service, the county shall consider the following factors:
(a) The county's risks in providing the service;
(b) The direct and indirect costs incurred by the county to provide the service;
(c) The consumers' ability to pay;
(d) The value received by the consumer;
(e) Pricing that would be needed to influence the level of demand for that service, if doing so would be in the interest of public policy; and
(f) The impact of providing the service on the county's employees, both singularly and in conjunction with other services.
(Ord. of 5-22-2025(2), § 1(Exh. A))

